X29870049</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>Metatranscriptome of iron mat microcosm - Mat ISCOC1; replicate 1; time: 10 minutes</TITLE><STUDY_REF accession="SRP511621"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP511621</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject">PRJNA1117470</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></STUDY_REF><DESIGN><DESIGN_DESCRIPTION>An Illumina Low Input (RNA) library was constructed and sequenced 2x151 using the Illumina NovaSeq platform. Raw reads were processed with BBDuk (version 39.01) to remove contaminants, trim adapter sequences, remove homopolymer tails with 5 Gs, and right quality trim reads where quality drops to 0. BBDuk was also used to remove reads that contained 1 or more 'N' bases, had an average quality score below 10, or had a minimum length &lt;51 bp. Reads mapped with BBMap to contaminants (human, cat, dog, mouse, common microbial contaminants, ribosomal RNA, or known spike-ins) were also removed</DESIGN_DESCRIPTION><SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR accession="SRS21513455"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS21513455</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN41570324</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_NAME>2105ISCOC1_1.10.1_MT</LIBRARY_NAME><LIBRARY_STRATEGY>RNA-Seq</LIBRARY_STRATEGY><LIBRARY_SOURCE>METATRANSCRIPTOMIC</LIBRARY_SOURCE><LIBRARY_SELECTION>other</LIBRARY_SELECTION><LIBRARY_LAYOUT><PAIRED/></LIBRARY_LAYOUT></LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR></DESIGN><PLATFORM><ILLUMINA><INSTRUMENT_MODEL>Illumina NovaSeq X</INSTRUMENT_MODEL></ILLUMINA></PLATFORM></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION lab_name="Earth Sciences" center_name="University of Delaware" accession="SRA2181357" alias="SUB15496401"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA2181357</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="University of Delaware">SUB15496401</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="institute"><Name>University of Delaware</Name><Address postal_code="19713"><Department>Earth Sciences</Department><Institution>University of Delaware</Institution><Street>590 Avenue 1743</St